PART 2 -- Q2: protection mechanism?  Does large |A| REMOVE the tuning, and at what cost?
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] Q2a  the split stiff/dust today = |C|/(2|A|) is INDEPENDENT of M and f (both densities carry the same M^2/3f^2), so tuning the gravitational scale M or the affine slope f cannot alter the ratio -- the only lever on |C|/|A| is A and C themselves (reaffirms L84 F1)   (stiff/dust = |C|/(2|A|), M- and f-independent)
